  era: "Section 7 \xB7 Mauryan Empire \xB7 c. 321 \u2013 185 BCE"
  title: Ashoka's Dhamma
  text: 'Ashoka''s Dhamma was a moral code: respect for elders, kindness to servants and animals, tolerance of all sects and restraint in speech. He appointed dhamma-mahamattas to spread it and sent missions abroad, including his son Mahinda to Sri Lanka.'
